  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/myxocyprinus-asiaticus-2/",
      "html": "<p>The Chinese Whimple Carp, sometimes called the Batman-Loach, is available almost anytime. Sadly the species is in danger of extinction in the wild, mainly due to hydroelectric power stations. All specimens traded come from aquaculture and are bred in captivity.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/myxocyprinus-asiaticus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Usually the fish come from Singapore, but as a test some were ordered from a new supplier in Hong Kong. The fish were observed carefully and two different phenotypes were found. Some specimens are reddish and the mighty dorsal fin is rounded at its tip. Others are rather black-and-white and the dorsal fin of these fish is much more pointed. Both phenotypes can be found in fish of the same size; the photographed ones are both 10-12 cm long. Do these differences in coloration represent the different sexes? That would be astonishing, as all whimple carps in the trade are still small juveniles.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/myxocyprinus-asiaticus-2/",
      "html": "<p>This fish can attain a maximum length of about 1.2 metres and a weight of about 23 kg; the adults look totally different, too. Due to their maximum size only juveniles can be kept in normal sized home aquaria. Later the fish have to move into really big tanks or garden ponds. The two photographed fish will be placed in a 5,000 litre tank to see how they develop.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/myxocyprinus-asiaticus-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species is winter-hardy in central Europe. They are much sought after to be kept along with koi carps, as Myxocyprinus is an algae eater and helps to keep the pond clean.</p>"
    }
  ],
